{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SYTEncodingBridgeTwo","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.OVTopAssembly","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RSKBurnsideTarget"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.substrate_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.substrate_witness","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RSKBurnsideDischarge.lean#L75-L79","doc":"The concrete witness the abstract substrate axiom asked for, now unconditional\n(`RSKBurnsideTarget.rskBurnside_imp_substrate` applied to the theorem above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.rskBurnsideHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.rskBurnsideHolds","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RSKBurnsideDischarge.lean#L51-L73","doc":"**`RSKBurnsideHolds`, conditional on `SnIsotypicSpechtSplit`**: `∑_{p ⊢ n} dimSYT p ² = n!`.\n\nReindex the `PartitionIndex` form of the RSK sum-of-squares along `partitionEquivYoungIndex`,\nconverting each summand with the SYT-encoding bridge.\n\n**Scope (corrected 2026-08-23).** This carries a class hypothesis and so proves the *implication*;\nthe docstring above previously read \"is now a theorem\", which overclaims a conditional proof\n(conditional-proved ≠ premise-established). Note also the direction: this derives the identity\n*from* the Wedderburn split. The **unconditional** theorem is `QOU.Mathlib.rskBurnsideHolds`, proved\nfrom the Robinson–Schensted correspondence with no hypothesis, and it is what\n`SnIsotypicSpechtSplitInstance` is built from — so citing this one as the source of the identity\nwould be circular. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.dimSYT_eq_numSYT","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.dimSYT_eq_numSYT","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RSKBurnsideDischarge.lean#L45-L49","doc":"`dimSYT` in the 0-indexed count, via the encoding bridge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.diagram_partitionEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RSKBurnsideDischarge.diagram_partitionEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RSKBurnsideDischarge.lean#L40-L43","doc":"The index equiv's forward map produces exactly the shape `dimSYT` counts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}